<title>USA: Jamaica buys 6,500 T PL-480 rice for October-agent.</title>
<headline>Jamaica buys 6,500 T PL-480 rice for October-agent.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jamaica bought 6,500 tonnes of U.S. long grain No.5 brown rice in bulk under the U.S. PL-480 export program, its U.S. export agent said.</p>
<p>The rice, purchased on August 15, was slated for October 5-25 delivery.</p>
<p>The rice was divided into two shipments of 3,250 tonnes each. One lot was purchased at $320.09 a tonne and another at $323.35 a tonne, all from Louis Dreyfus, FOB, U.S. Gulf of Mexico, the agent said.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
